{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.089,
            0.408,
            0.107
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "At a Glance"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.12,
            0.876,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "The cell is the basic structural and functional unit of all living organisms."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.157,
            0.876,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "Prokaryotic cells do not have a well-defined nucleus, instead their genetic material is present in a region called the nucleoid. They also lack membrane-bound organelles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.212,
            0.875,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "Eukaryotic cells are larger and more complex. They have a welldefined nucleus and several membrane-bound organelles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.25,
            0.876,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "All cells are surrounded by a cell membrane. In addition, cells of plants, fungi and bacteria have a cell wall outside the cell membrane."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.079,
            0.347,
            0.183,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.304,
            0.876,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "The nucleus of eukaryotic cells contains chromosomes, which are composed of DNA and associated proteins, which carry genetic information."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.358,
            0.876,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": "All cells are filled with cytoplasm. In eukaryotic cells, cytoplasm contains  several  cell  organelles,  each  performing  a  specific  function."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.396,
            0.875,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "Important cell organelles include the nucleus, endoplasmic reticulum, mitochondria, golgi apparatus, ribosomes and lysosomes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.433,
            0.875,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "Plant cells also contain special organelles called plastids, such as chloroplasts, leucoplasts and chromoplasts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.471,
            0.838,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": "Mitosis produces two daughter cells identical to the parent cell."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.491,
            0.876,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "Meiosis is a two-step division process which produces four daughter cells, each having half the number of chromosomes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.529,
            0.876,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "Normal cells grow in a controlled manner, perform their functions and die naturally, while cancer cells lose control and keep dividing uncontrollably leading to the formation of tumours."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.461,
            0.674,
            0.768,
            0.696
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Revise, Reflect, Refine"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.738,
            0.888,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "1. Differentiate between the following pairs of terms based on the clues given in parentheses:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.774,
            0.684,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "(i) Cell membrane and cell wall (permeability)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.794,
            0.513,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "(ii) RER and SER (structure)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.813,
            0.673,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Chloroplasts and chromoplasts (pigments)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.835,
            0.808,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": "2. Two similar animal cells are placed in two different solutions:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.859,
            0.547,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "y Cell X is placed in pure water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.879,
            0.691,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "y Cell Y is placed in a concentrated salt solution."
        },
        {
